 "review": {
  "score": 5.0,
  "round": 1,
  "problems": [
   "Scale: in the 'in a place' and 'wide' frames the volcano is only about 1.3\u20131.5\u00d7 the person's height, so it reads as a large prop, not 'scenery much taller than a person'",
   "The two lava streams are thin, wobbly strips with round ember dots at the ends (-40,-157) and (50,-193), so they read as dangling stick legs with feet, like a skeleton, not lava flowing down a slope",
   "The smoke is 4 stacked, fairly opaque round ellipses (alpha 0.85/0.75/0.6) in a vertical column. It reads as a pile of grey stones or a snowman sitting on the crater, not a soft plume",
   "The lowest smoke ellipse (y -372, ry 22) and the ember glow (y -360) cover the crater rim, so the gold rim and molten crater get lost",
   "The silhouette is a tall narrow spike (top width 96 against base 400, height 335), more like a chimney or termite mound than a broad volcano"
  ]
 },
